cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the accompanying preprint."
title: "Bayesian model: Gaussian Process prediction of UV-Vis lambda_max with benchmark vs TD-DFT"
abstract: >-
  Jupyter-notebook workflow and data for the manuscript "Benchmark Label
  Definition, Not Model Capability, Explains a Machine-Learning Advantage over
  TD-DFT for λmax Prediction". Curates the Beard et al. (2019) literature-mined
  UV-Vis dataset, trains a Gaussian Process on 256-bit Morgan fingerprints plus
  largest conjugated-system size, and evaluates it against TD-DFT / sTDA under
  leakage-free and Bemis-Murcko scaffold-split protocols, plus two independent
  external corpora and published quantum-chemical benchmarks.
keywords:
  - UV-Vis absorption
  - lambda_max
  - Gaussian process
  - machine learning
  - TD-DFT
  - benchmark
  - chemical space
  - reproducibility
